# Tools installed INTO the deb-builder image (kiosk-deb-builder).
#
# BUILD-TIME ONLY — none of these ship in the kiosk image. What goes into the
# shipped image is os-builder/rootfs-packages.list instead.
#
# This is the hand-edited INPUT (names only). After changing it run
#   make builder-update
# which resolves it against the pinned Debian snapshot and regenerates
#   lock/packages-version-lock.list   (exact pkg=version)
#   lock/packages-hash-lock.txt       (sha256 of every .deb)
# Those locks are what actually get installed, and are verified at image-build
# time — so a toolchain bump shows up as a reviewable commit diff.

# --- compile + package the Electron app ---
# From NodeSource, not Debian. The exact version is derived from .nvmrc and
# rewritten in place by packages-update, so this line is generated — edit
# .nvmrc and re-run `make builder-update` instead of editing it here.
# NodeSource's nodejs bundles corepack (which provisions the yarn named by
# app/package.json packageManager), so Debian's node-corepack is not used.

nodejs=24.15.0-1nodesource1
dpkg-dev            # dpkg-deb, used by electron-forge's maker-deb
fakeroot            # lets maker-deb stage root-owned files without being root

# --- support ---

ca-certificates     # HTTPS to the npm registry for `yarn install`
git                 # electron-forge pulls @electron/node-gyp from a git URL
curl                # used by yarn/corepack to fetch the pinned yarn release
xz-utils            # electron distributions are xz-compressed
